From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meta-xuantie <noreply@xuantie.invalid>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sysconfig: append STAGING_LIBDIR/python-sysconfigdata to
 sys.path

So that the target configuration can be used when running the native
interpreter during cross builds.

This is the Python 3.13 port of oe-core's
0001-distutils-sysconfig-append-STAGING_LIBDIR-python-sys.patch. In 3.13
the sysconfig module became a package (Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py) and
_init_posix() grew an upstream cross-build branch keyed on the new
_PYTHON_SYSCONFIGDATA_PATH env var. oe-core's python3targetconfig.bbclass
still only exports _PYTHON_SYSCONFIGDATA_NAME="_sysconfigdata" and relies
on the target sysconfigdata being reachable via sys.path, so without this
the native python raises "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named
'_sysconfigdata'" for every recipe that inherits setuptools3-base /
python3targetconfig (btrfs-tools, ...).

Add a STAGING_LIBDIR fallback branch that mirrors the langdale patch,
placed after the upstream _PYTHON_SYSCONFIGDATA_PATH branch so the newer
mechanism still wins when set.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-core specific; python 3.13 backport]

---
 Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py
+++ b/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py
@@ -357,6 +357,13 @@ def _init_posix(vars):
         spec = FileFinder(path, (SourceFileLoader, SOURCE_SUFFIXES)).find_spec(name)
         _temp = module_from_spec(spec)
         spec.loader.exec_module(_temp)
+    elif 'STAGING_LIBDIR' in os.environ:
+        # OE cross build: target sysconfigdata lives in the target sysroot.
+        # Append it to sys.path so `import _sysconfigdata` resolves the target
+        # build config when running the native interpreter. Kept off PYTHONPATH
+        # for the reason noted above.
+        sys.path.append(os.environ['STAGING_LIBDIR'] + '/python-sysconfigdata')
+        _temp = __import__(name, globals(), locals(), ['build_time_vars'], 0)
     else:
         _temp = __import__(name, globals(), locals(), ['build_time_vars'], 0)
     build_time_vars = _temp.build_time_vars
